Tom: I want to learn how to help a choking person. My uncle once choked on a fish bone.
Lucy: That sounds really useful. I''d like to learn how to treat burns.
Tom: Why burns?
Lucy: My little sister once burnt her hand on a hot pan, and I didn''t know what to do.
Tom: I see. Then this club is perfect for both of us.
Lucy: Yes. The teacher said we will also learn how to call for an ambulance.
Tom: Great. Let''s sign up together after class.', 'Lucy 问 Tom 最想学哪项急救;Tom 想学帮噎住的人,因为叔叔曾被鱼刺噎住;Lucy 想学处理烧伤,因为妹妹曾被热锅烫伤而自己不知所措;两人决定一起报名,还会学怎么叫救护车。', 'uk_female', '[{"q":"Which first-aid skill does Tom want to learn most?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["How to help a choking person.","How to treat a burn.","How to stop bleeding.","How to set a broken arm."]},{"q":"Why does Tom choose that skill?","type":"choice","answer":"B","options":["His teacher told him to.","His uncle once choked on a fish bone.","It is the easiest to learn.","He saw it in a film."]},{"q":"What does Lucy want to learn?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["How to treat burns.","How to swim.","How to drive a car.","How to cook fish."]},{"q":"What happened to Lucy''s little sister?","type":"choice","answer":"B","options":["She fell off a bike.","She burnt her hand on a hot pan.","She caught a cold.","She was bitten by a dog."]},{"q":"What else will the club teach them?","type":"choice","answer":"C","options":["How to play football.","How to write a story.","How to call for an ambulance.","How to sell medicine."]}]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, 'long', 'elective2', 'U5');
In China, you can call one-two-zero for an ambulance.
In the United States, people call nine-one-one for any emergency.
In the United Kingdom, the number is nine-nine-nine.
When you call, stay calm and tell the operator clearly where you are and what has happened.', '不同国家有不同的急救电话:在中国拨120叫救护车;在美国拨911处理任何紧急情况;在英国是999;打电话时要保持冷静,清楚地告诉接线员你在哪里、发生了什么。', 'uk_female', '[{"q":"What is the main idea of the passage?","type":"choice","answer":"D","options":["All countries use the same number.","Emergency numbers are only for fun.","You should never call for help.","Different countries use different emergency numbers."]},{"q":"Which number do you call for an ambulance in China?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["120.","911.","999.","112."]},{"q":"What number is used in the United States?","type":"choice","answer":"B","options":["120.","911.","999.","000."]},{"q":"What should you do when you call?","type":"choice","answer":"C","options":["Hang up quickly.","Shout as loud as you can.","Stay calm and explain clearly.","Give a false name."]},{"q":"What two things should you tell the operator?","type":"choice","answer":"D","options":["Your favourite food and colour.","Your age and your school.","The weather and the time.","Where you are and what has happened."]}]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, 'short', 'elective2', 'U5');
Anna: Stay calm, Mark. Let me see. It''s red but not too deep.
Mark: It really hurts. Should I put some butter on it?
Anna: No, never put butter on a burn. That keeps the heat in.
Mark: So what should I do?
Anna: Hold your arm under cool running water for about ten minutes.
Mark: That feels much better already.
Anna: Good. Then we''ll cover it loosely with a clean cloth. If it gets worse, we''ll go to hospital.', 'Mark 在灶台上烫伤了胳膊,慌忙叫 Anna;Anna 让他冷静,查看后说不深;Mark 问能否抹黄油,Anna 说绝不能,会把热留住;她让他把胳膊放凉水下冲约十分钟,Mark 感觉好多了;之后用干净布宽松地盖住,若加重就去医院。', 'uk_female', '[{"q":"How did Mark hurt himself?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["He burnt his arm on the cooker.","He cut his finger with a knife.","He fell down the stairs.","He sprained his wrist."]},{"q":"What does Mark first think of putting on the burn?","type":"choice","answer":"B","options":["Cool water.","Butter.","A bandage.","Some ice."]},{"q":"Why does Anna say not to use butter?","type":"choice","answer":"C","options":["It is too expensive.","It smells bad.","It keeps the heat in the burn.","It washes the burn away."]},{"q":"What does Anna tell Mark to do?","type":"choice","answer":"D","options":["Rub the burn hard.","Wrap it very tightly.","Go straight to bed.","Hold it under cool running water."]},{"q":"What will they do if the burn gets worse?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["Go to hospital.","Put more butter on it.","Do nothing at all.","Cover it with oil."]}]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, 'long', 'elective2', 'U5');
First, make sure the person really cannot speak or breathe.
Stand behind the person and wrap your arms around the waist.
Make a fist and push up into the stomach with quick movements.
Keep doing this until the food is forced out and the person can breathe again.', '海姆立克急救法是帮助噎住者的简单方法:先确认对方确实说不出话、不能呼吸;站到其身后,用双臂环住腰;握拳并用快速动作向上推压腹部;持续进行,直到食物被推出、对方重新能呼吸。', 'uk_female', '[{"q":"What is the Heimlich manoeuvre used for?","type":"choice","answer":"B","options":["To stop bleeding.","To help a choking person.","To cool a burn.","To treat a sprained ankle."]},{"q":"What should you check first?","type":"choice","answer":"C","options":["That the person has eaten enough.","That the room is warm.","That the person really cannot speak or breathe.","That an ambulance has come."]},{"q":"Where do you stand to do the manoeuvre?","type":"choice","answer":"D","options":["In front of the person.","Beside the door.","On a chair.","Behind the person."]},{"q":"How do you use your fist?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["You push up into the stomach.","You hold it on the person''s head.","You wave it in the air.","You press it on the chest."]},{"q":"When do you stop?","type":"choice","answer":"B","options":["After only one push.","When the food is forced out and the person can breathe.","When you feel tired.","When other people arrive."]}]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, 'short', 'elective2', 'U5');
Boy: My grandfather has fallen down and he isn''t moving!
Operator: Stay calm. Is he breathing?
Boy: I''m not sure. He looks very pale.
Operator: All right. Put him on his back and remove any pillows.
Boy: Okay, I''ve done that.
Operator: Now put your hand in the middle of his chest and press down, twice a second.
Boy: I''m pressing now. Please send someone quickly!
Operator: An ambulance is already on the way. Keep going until it arrives.', '接线员问发生了什么;男孩说爷爷摔倒了,不动了;接线员让他冷静,问是否在呼吸;男孩说不确定、爷爷脸色很苍白;接线员指导他让爷爷仰卧、移开枕头,把手放在胸部中央每秒按压两次;男孩照做并请求快点派人;接线员说救护车已在路上,让他坚持到车来。', 'uk_female', '[{"q":"Why does the boy call the emergency services?","type":"choice","answer":"C","options":["His house is on fire.","He has lost his way home.","His grandfather has fallen and isn''t moving.","He has burnt his hand."]},{"q":"What does the operator ask first?","type":"choice","answer":"D","options":["The boy''s name.","The boy''s home address only.","What the boy had for dinner.","Whether his grandfather is breathing."]},{"q":"What does the operator tell the boy to do with his grandfather?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["Put him on his back and remove any pillows.","Make him sit up in a chair.","Give him some water.","Carry him outside."]},{"q":"How often should the boy press on the chest?","type":"choice","answer":"B","options":["Once a minute.","Twice a second.","Only one time.","Every ten seconds."]},{"q":"What does the operator say about the ambulance?","type":"choice","answer":"C","options":["It cannot come tonight.","The boy must drive it himself.","It is already on the way.","It will come tomorrow."]}]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, 'long', 'elective2', 'U5');
First, stay calm and do not panic, even if the person is badly hurt.
Second, make sure that the place is safe before you help.
Third, call for help early, and never be afraid to ask for an ambulance.
If you follow these rules, your quick action may save someone''s life.', '给急救时要记住三条简单原则:第一,保持冷静、别惊慌,哪怕伤者伤得很重;第二,在施救前确认现场安全;第三,尽早求助,别害怕叫救护车。遵守这些原则,你的迅速行动也许能救人一命。', 'uk_female', '[{"q":"How many rules does the speaker give?","type":"choice","answer":"D","options":["Five.","Four.","Two.","Three."]},{"q":"What is the first rule?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["Stay calm and do not panic.","Run away at once.","Wait for an hour.","Shout for a long time."]},{"q":"What should you check before helping?","type":"choice","answer":"B","options":["The time of day.","That the place is safe.","The price of medicine.","The colour of the sky."]},{"q":"What does the third rule say?","type":"choice","answer":"C","options":["Never call anyone.","Help only your family.","Call for help early and ask for an ambulance.","Keep the problem a secret."]},{"q":"What may your quick action do?","type":"choice","answer":"D","options":["Waste a lot of time.","Make people angry.","Cost too much money.","Save someone''s life."]}]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, 'short', 'elective2', 'U5');

